==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|attercoppe}}, from {{inh|en|ang|ātorcoppe|t=spider}} (> {{cog|gmq-oda|etærkop}}, {{m|gmq-oda|ederkoppæ}} > {{cog|da|edderkop||spider}}), corresponding to {{compound|en|atter|gloss1=poison, venom|cop|gloss2=spider}}. The latter is still to be found in the English word {{m|en|cobweb}}. Cognate to Dutch {{m|nl|etterkop|t=peevish or ill-natured person}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈætəkɒp/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# ''(obsolete except pike
 dialects)'' A [[spider]].
# ''(obsolete except in dialects)'' A [[peevish]] or [[ill-natured]] person.

